  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under refill protocol RBC-RX-05. All 7 messages (6 at the start, 1 that arrived during the review) were decided and closed. Three new results/documents arrived mid-review (§7) and changed decisions; those corrections are recorded in a note for each patient.\n\npt-0027 Frank Odum, lisinopril 10 mg: renewed at first (90 days + 1 refill). The August outside potassium of 5.9 was on a hemolyzed sample, so it didn't count, and a repeat BMP was ordered (sr-t0002). Then a new valid outside BMP arrived (collected 10/20, potassium 5.8). I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0001) before anything was dispensed. No refill, pending review: urgent task to you (task-t0020, focus mr-00283). The patient got a corrected message with potassium precautions. The repeat BMP order is still open.\n\npt-0030 Samuel Price:\n- Metformin 1000 mg BID: renewed 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0004). The patient's request and both pharmacy requests were treated as one request. eGFR is now 58 after the lab's correction (still at least 45), and HbA1c was 7.1% at an outside lab on 8/19.\n- Lisinopril 20 mg: renewed at first. Then the lab corrected the 10/6 creatinine to 1.49, 35% above the 1.10 before the 9/18 dose increase. The protocol treats a rise over 30% like a potassium of 5.5 or higher. I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0003). Urgent task to you (task-t0021, focus mr-00295). The patient got a corrected message.\n\npt-0031 Marcus Webb:\n- Metformin 500 mg BID: renewed 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0007). The 10/14 eGFR of 39 was entered in error and doesn't count; valid eGFR 92 and HbA1c 6.9% on 9/28.\n- Lisinopril 10 mg: there was no BMP in the past 12 months, so I first gave a 30-day supply with no refills and ordered a BMP (sr-t0006). A valid BMP then arrived (collected 10/22, potassium 4.6), so I replaced the order with 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0019). The patient was told no further blood test is needed. The BMP order sr-t0006 is no longer needed, but I had no tool to cancel it.\n\nEach patient got a reply and then a correction or update message; notes are doc-t0025, doc-t0026 and doc-t0027. The three results-queue items that arrived (inbox-a0001, a0002, a0004) are still open for your review, because you asked me to clear only the messages queue.",
